Real Options - Introduction
14
Valuation of Call Option
  Call option pays max[P-60,0] at the end of the year
 either 80-60 = 20 or 0 at the end of the year
  Replicate this payoff distribution by taking a position in Enron stock and the risk free asset: 
X*50 + Y*1.1 = 0
X*80 + Y*1.1 = 20
Solution: X = 2/3, Y = -30.30 
Value of option V = X*60 + Y*1 = 2*60/3 - 30.30 = 9.7 

